Chapter: TcpChecksumRefuse
  cites Net chapter NetworkStack
  cites Net chapter Tcp
  cites Net chapter Ethernet
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 We say:

Section: Wire Fixtures
  srv-mac : List Integer = [82, 84, 0, 18, 52, 86]
  cli-mac : List Integer = [82, 85, 10, 0, 2, 2]
  srv-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 15]
  cli-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 100]
  gw-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 2]

  psh : Integer = bit-or tcp-flag-psh tcp-flag-ack
  get-bytes : List Integer = [71, 69, 84, 32, 47, 32, 72, 84, 84, 80, 47, 49, 46, 49, 13, 10, 13, 10]

 corrupt-at flips one bit in one byte AFTER tcp-with-checksum has run, so the
 stored field is correct for the bytes the sender had and wrong for the bytes
 the receiver gets. That is the shape of the PR 64 DMA truncation this check
 exists to catch, and it is the only difference between the two arms.

  corrupt-at : List Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  corrupt-at (bytes) (i) = list-set-at bytes i (bit-xor (list-at bytes i) 1)

  mk-frame : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  mk-frame (seq) (ack) (flags) (payload) (flip) =
    let seg = tcp-with-checksum (tcp-build-segment 50000 80 seq ack flags 8192 payload) cli-ip srv-ip
    in let wire = if flip < 0 then seg else corrupt-at seg flip
    in let ip = ip-build-packet cli-ip srv-ip ip-proto-tcp wire
    in eth-build-frame srv-mac cli-mac eth-type-ipv4 ip

  c-syn : List Integer = mk-frame 1000 0 tcp-flag-syn [] (0 - 1)

Section: Server Session
  srv0 : NetSession = net-session-new srv-mac srv-ip gw-ip 80 0 cli-ip 5000
  listening : NetSession = (net-listen srv0).session
  established : NetSession = (net-process-frame listening c-syn).session

 The outbox is cleared because the handshake left its SYN-ACK in it. Counting
 an uncleared outbox would report 1 for both arms and discriminate nothing,
 which is the assertion this arm exists to make.

  base : NetSession = set-outbox established []

Section: The Two Arms

 The control is not decoration. A checker that refuses everything and a checker
 that works are indistinguishable on the corrupt arm alone, which is the whole
 reason the absence of this check was invisible.

  clean-frame : List Integer = mk-frame 1001 5001 psh get-bytes (0 - 1)
  dirty-frame : List Integer = mk-frame 1001 5001 psh get-bytes 24

  clean-result : NetResult = net-process-frame base clean-frame
  dirty-result : NetResult = net-process-frame base dirty-frame

 The IP header carries its own checksum and its own arm. Byte 16 is the first
 byte of the source address, inside the twenty ip-header-valid sums.

  bad-ip-frame : List Integer =
    let ip = ip-build-packet cli-ip srv-ip ip-proto-tcp (tcp-with-checksum (tcp-build-segment 50000 80 1001 5001 psh 8192 get-bytes) cli-ip srv-ip)
    in eth-build-frame srv-mac cli-mac eth-type-ipv4 (corrupt-at ip 16)

  bad-ip-result : NetResult = net-process-frame base bad-ip-frame

 A truncated receive is the arm the checksum cannot cover, because the checksum
 is computed over the bytes that ARRIVED and the header is one of them. Before
 ip-header-valid tested the length this frame took the guest down with EXC=06.

  take : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  take (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else take xs (i + 1) n (list-push acc (list-at xs i))

  cut-frame : List Integer = take clean-frame 0 (list-length clean-frame - 6) []
  cut-result : NetResult = net-process-frame base cut-frame

Section: Entry
  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("clean-verdict=" & (clean-result.output))
    print-line-uni ("clean-bytes=" & show (list-length (clean-result.data)))
    print-line-uni ("dirty-verdict=" & (dirty-result.output))
    print-line-uni ("dirty-bytes=" & show (list-length (dirty-result.data)))
    print-line-uni ("clean-emitted=" & show (list-length ((clean-result.session).outbox)))
    print-line-uni ("dirty-emitted=" & show (list-length ((dirty-result.session).outbox)))
    print-line-uni ("bad-ip-verdict=" & (bad-ip-result.output))
    print-line-uni ("cut-verdict=" & (cut-result.output))
    print-line-uni ("cut-bytes=" & show (list-length (cut-result.data)))
    print-line-uni ("checksum-valid-clean=" & show (tcp-checksum-valid (tcp-with-checksum (tcp-build-segment 50000 80 1001 5001 psh 8192 get-bytes) cli-ip srv-ip) cli-ip srv-ip))
    print-line-uni ("checksum-valid-zero=" & show (tcp-checksum-valid (tcp-build-segment 50000 80 1001 5001 psh 8192 get-bytes) cli-ip srv-ip))
  end
